# Upstream base for the locally-built
# jenkins-plugin_oracle-cloud-infrastructure-compute_*.hpi in this directory.
#
# This plugin is a FORK of the upstream repo, carrying patches from unmerged
# upstream PRs that we require. It is installed from the bundled .hpi (see the
# "ensure local plugins" task), NOT from the Jenkins update center, so Renovate
# cannot bump the artifact itself.
#
# Renovate watches upstream RELEASES via the marker below. When a newer upstream
# release exists, it opens a PR bumping upstream_base_version. That PR is a
# NOTIFICATION, not a drop-in update:
#
#   1. Check whether our required PRs have merged upstream (if so, consider
#      dropping the fork and returning this plugin to the normal manifest).
#   2. Rebase our patches onto the new upstream tag.
#   3. Rebuild the .hpi and replace jenkins-plugin_oracle-cloud-infrastructure-compute_*.hpi.
#   4. Commit the rebuilt .hpi onto the SAME Renovate branch, THEN merge.
#
# NEVER merge the marker bump on its own: doing so desyncs this recorded base
# from the deployed artifact. The PR carries the "do-not-merge/hold" label, which
# Tide enforces, so the PR cannot merge until someone removes the hold.
#
# renovate: datasource=github-releases depName=jenkinsci/oracle-cloud-infrastructure-compute-plugin
upstream_base_version=1.0.21
